# Product terminology

Burn & Build uses **three terms for three layers**. Do not swap them for the same concept.

## Questionnaire vs intake (locked decision)

The multi-step flow that collects body, activity, and lifestyle answers before checkout has **one product name** and **one internal data name**. Do not use them interchangeably in user-facing copy.

| Context | Term | Examples |
|---------|------|----------|
| **User-facing process / page** | **Questionnaire** (or **program questionnaire**) | Nav, docs, support copy, “go back to the questionnaire”, waiver (“results of this questionnaire”) |
| **URL / folder** | **`/questionnaire/`** | Locked path — do not rename to `/intake/` |
| **Code / data model** | **`intake`** | `pkg.intake`, `intake-form` CSS classes, `intakeDate` — internal only, not a user-facing label |
| **Avoid as primary label** | **Intake form** | Do not use as the page title or marketing name unless the user explicitly requests a rebrand |

**Rule:** Say **questionnaire** to users and in agent/docs copy; say **`intake`** only in code when referring to the saved answers object or form markup.

## One-sentence rule

> **Burn & Build Diet** is the product; **your program** is what we generate; **your food plan** is what you eat.

## Three layers

| Term | Layer | Question it answers | Use for |
|------|--------|---------------------|---------|
| **Diet** | Product | What do they buy? | *The Burn & Build Diet*, *Get the Diet*, heritage (*Since 1982*), pricing ($149), checkout (*Download your Burn & Build Diet*), brand positioning |
| **Food plan** | Eating rules | What do they follow daily? | PDF page 3, servings prescription, meal-building steps, handbook/FAQ about portions and adherence |
| **Program** | Generated package | What did the engine produce? | Questionnaire → Burn Engine → **program report** PDF; saved account artifact; *your program will be created* before Stripe |

## Avoid

| Wrong | Why |
|-------|-----|
| **Food program** | Not a product term — drop entirely |
| **Diet plan** | Merges product (*diet*) with eating rules (*food plan*) — use **diet** or **food plan** or **program** by layer |
| **Diet program** | Same merge — pick **diet** or **program** |
| Using **diet**, **food plan**, and **program** interchangeably for the same thing | Each layer has one primary term |
| **Intake form** as the user-facing name for `/questionnaire/` | Use **questionnaire** / **program questionnaire** — **intake** is code-only |

## Correct examples

- Landing CTA: **Get the Diet** → `/questionnaire/?create=1`
- Questionnaire page title: **Program Questionnaire** (tag: *Burn & Build program questionnaire*)
- Pricing product name: **The Burn & Build Diet** — $149 one-time purchase
- Before checkout: *When you have answered these questions… your **program** will be created*
- Sample / Welcome section title: **Food Plan** (PDF page 3 — eating rules, not the product name)
- Print Shop / PDF document: **Program Report** (full multi-page deliverable)
- FAQ (all three in one sentence): *Bring your **food plan** and **program report** to your doctor before starting **the diet**.*

## Common mistakes (fix when editing copy)

| Surface | Wrong | Right |
|---------|-------|-------|
| Questionnaire step label | Build Your **Diet Plan** | Build Your **Program** or start-your-**diet** wording — never *diet plan* |
| Questionnaire page title | **Intake form** | **Program Questionnaire** (or **Questionnaire** in short nav copy) |
| Questionnaire intro | Burn Engine builds your **diet** | builds your **program** (report + planner) |
| Download button | Download **diet plan** | Download **program report** or **your diet** (product) |
| Pricing disclaimer | difficult **program** | difficult **diet** (product) |
| Program shell / library | Go to your **diet**; Your **diet plans** | **program** / **programs** |
| Welcome (whole report) | a **food plan** built only for you | a **program** built only for you |
| Projections intro | **food program** | **program** or **food plan** — never *food program* |

## Gray areas (usually OK)

- **Program report** — document name for the full PDF; not the product name, not page 3 alone
- **`intake` in code** — saved answers object (`pkg.intake`); not a user-facing synonym for questionnaire
- Colloquial **plan** when context is clearly servings or adherence (*your plan uses servings*) — not the product name
- Waiver / everyday English (*changes to my diet*) — eating habits, not product naming
- **Cutting-diet staples** — historical bodybuilding term in food-list copy
- Locked KWarner user-authored lines — do not reauthor; flag only if user requests a terminology pass (see `.cursor/rules/user-authored-copy.mdc`)

## Agent checklist

1. Which layer is this copy about — **product**, **eating rules**, or **generated package**?
2. Pick **diet**, **food plan**, or **program** accordingly — one primary term per layer
3. For the pre-checkout wizard: user-facing **questionnaire**; code **`intake`** only
4. Never introduce **food program** or **diet plan**
5. When fixing drift, change **only** what the user explicitly asks for — one surface at a time
